## Part 2 — Provider Grading System

### Rating Dimensions (5 axes, A–D scale)

| Dimension | What it measures |
|-----------|-----------------|
| **Accuracy** | WER, language fidelity, hallucination control |
| **Latency** | Time-to-first-audio — target total pipeline <800ms |
| **Naturalness** | Voice prosody, code-switching fluency, human-likeness |
| **Reliability** | Uptime, error handling, free tier stability |
| **Cost** | How far the free tier goes (~100 test calls/month = ~50 hrs STT) |

### Grade Scale
| Grade | Label | Meaning |
|-------|-------|---------|
| 🏆 **A+** | GOLD STANDARD | Ship to any client immediately. Best in class. |
| 🟢 **A** | OPTIMAL | Production-ready. Negligible tradeoffs. |
| 🔵 **B** | GOOD | Reliable. Minor tradeoffs acceptable for most use cases. |
| 🟡 **C** | CAUTION | Works but notable limitation. Testing/non-critical use only. |
| 🔴 **D** | AVOID | Significant technical or UX limitation. Do not ship. |
| ⚫ **X** | INCOMPATIBLE | Technical blocker. Will not function correctly. |

